+| D-23 | No token expiry; no second factor; an admin never acts as a member. | A machine's token lives until rotated or revoked; every admin act is audited in their own name. | A stolen token lives until noticed; last-seen times are the signal. |
+| D-24 | Disabling and withdrawing are reversible and delete nothing; erasure is `serve purge entry\|memory … --yes` by the operator with a shell, audited, covering the row, the revisions, the feed's payload reference and the mirror's files, durable against a re-send; no API route erases. | What a person asks to have erased must not come back from a copy. | A purge rebuilds the repositories the entry touched, beside the server. |
